    "guidance": "Use only as a closely monitored attached-transport option, not as the default. In validation from its own demonstrated entry states, h01 met the fixed final exit in 5/12 runs; successful runs first met it at steps 184–225 and ended with the block inside and drawer_position 0.296–0.300. Its documented intended use is an open, stable drawer with reliable object_pose, closed fingers, two causal frames showing common block/TCP motion, and a feasible arm posture; the object-frame design is appropriate in principle for a plausibly held, displaced block, but displacement benefit has no out-of-distribution rollout evidence. Avoid uncertain attachment, unreliable pose, premature-drop recovery, or post-release/handle motion. The seven validation failures comprised six final outside-cavity states and one inside state with drawer_position 0.205; watch for block/TCP decoupling before the cavity, abrupt relative-pose change, off-cavity settling, drawer_position falling to <=0.26, extreme object motion, or persistent IK/limit diagnostics. After two frames show an inside, floor-height, stationary block detached from the opened gripper, switch to h02 for destination/handle anchoring, or h03 if release phase remains locally ambiguous. Hand close_drawer only that verified deposit state, preferably with the free gripper at the handle approach."
